{"id": "a58d7852-238c-42a4-a2e4-5d09acfed15e", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Got the methodology loaded. Now let me gather the actual data on the `telemetry-pipeline` stack — this requires checking CloudFormation resources, compute, data stores, networking, and backups across layers, which is exactly the kind of multi-service, multi-call lookup I shouldn't pull into this chat directly.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_e0eAunzXzxhY0Dz21eYkjr", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"deep_research": true, "prompt": "{
  "task": "Run a resilience data-gathering pass for the CloudFormation stack named 'telemetry-pipeline' in eu-west-1, to answer: what survives an Availability Zone failure, and what survives a Region failure, today.",
  "context": "User ingests device telemetry via this stack in eu-west-1 and wants to know what happens to the pipeline on an AZ failure or a full eu-west-1 Region failure, and what to fix first. I (the chat agent) am writing the final resilience report myself using the resilience-review skill's report format — your job is ONLY to gather read-only facts, not to write conclusions, a roadmap, or prose recommendations.",
  "resources": ["CloudFormation stack: telemetry-pipeline", "Region: eu-west-1"],
  "method": "Use cloudformation:ListStackResources on the 'telemetry-pipeline' stack to enumerate every resource. Group them into layers: entry/routing (load balancers, API Gateway, CloudFront, Route 53), compute (EC2/ASG, ECS, EKS, Lambda, Step Functions), data (RDS/Aurora, DynamoDB, ElastiCache, DocumentDB, Neptune, Redshift, OpenSearch), storage (EBS, EFS, FSx, S3), messaging/events (SQS, SNS, Kinesis, MSK, EventBridge), identity (Cognito), and shared dependencies (VPC/subnets/NAT gateways/VPC endpoints/VPN/Direct Connect, Secrets Manager, KMS keys, ECR images, certificates). For each resource run the specific read-only checks for its service type (e.g. for Kinesis: kinesis:DescribeStreamSummary for mode/retention; for DynamoDB: DescribeContinuousBackups for PITR status + ListBackups + DescribeTable replicas, noting PITR is NOT the account-level flag; for Lambda: GetFunction or GetFunctionConfiguration + ListEventSourceMappings; for EC2/ASG: DescribeAutoScalingGroups for AZ spread, DescribeImages for AMI existence in eu-west-1 and in a candidate recovery region; for RDS/Aurora: DescribeDBInstances for MultiAZ/BackupRetentionPeriod/ReadReplicas/DeletionProtection, DescribeDBClusters/DescribeGlobalClusters for Aurora Global Database; for S3: GetBucketVersioning + GetReplicationConfiguration; for SQS: GetQueueAttributes for RedrivePolicy/DLQ). Also check shared network single points that affect the AZ scenario: DescribeNatGateways + DescribeRouteTables (is each AZ's private subnet routed through a zonal NAT gateway in its own AZ, or one NAT gateway serving multiple AZs?), DescribeVpcEndpoints (interface endpoints in how many AZs). Check AWS Backup coverage: ListProtectedResources, ListRecoveryPointsByResource for resources in scope, and backup:DescribeRegionSettings to see if DynamoDB advanced features are on (needed for cross-Region DynamoDB backup copies). Check Secrets Manager (DescribeSecret for replica regions) and KMS keys used by any encrypted resource for presence of multi-Region keys or replicas. If a call is denied or the resource type isn't covered above, note it as not checked with the reason — do not guess.",
  "output_format": "Return ONLY data, one row per resource, in exactly this pipe-delimited format: layer | resource name/ARN | type | Region | in-Region redundancy (AZs, nodes, tasks) | backups (kind, frequency, retention) | copies/images/IaC outside the Region | point-in-time recovery | replication | what could not be read. Do not add a prose summary, conclusions, a roadmap, or recommendations — just the rows and a short list of any calls that were denied or skipped. If the stack does not exist under this exact name, say so and list the closest candidate CloudFormation stack names found in eu-west-1 instead of substituting one."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Map telemetry-pipeline CloudFormation stack in eu-west-1 and run read-only AZ/Region resilience checks per layer"}], "created_at": null}
